// `io.flush()` is nullary, and the checker arity-gates it like every other native. `io.flush(1)`
// hands an argument to a 0-parameter function, so the program is rejected before either backend
// runs rather than aborting once it reaches the call.
//
// The four writers in the same module each take exactly one value, so `flush` is the one place in
// `std.io` where the ctx dispatch resolves a name before the arity check the others share — which
// is the mistake this case is here to catch.
// expect: error E0007 at 12:1
// expect: exit 1
use std.io

io.flush(1)
echo "unreachable"
